# Darias Website — Cursor Rules

- Keep token use low. Be concise. No long reports after every step.
- Do not reread entire files repeatedly. Touch only files needed for a change.
- Do not rewrite working code without a reason.
- Do not add unnecessary dependencies, frameworks, or build systems.
- Make safe, reasonable decisions yourself. Do not ask for approval on every small technical choice.
- Do not leave TODOs or placeholders.
- Do not create non-working buttons or fake features.
- Do not invent users, downloads, ratings, reviews, emails, or URLs.
- Find the root cause first, then fix.
- Always keep responsive design. Never design desktop-only.
- Do not break the Turkish/English i18n structure.
- Keep GitHub Pages compatibility. Use static directories. No Windows/local absolute paths.
- No backend, database, secrets, or API keys.
- No unnecessary refactors.
- Never use `git push --force` unless the user explicitly demands it. Default: never force push.
- Goal: production-ready static website.

## Stack
- HTML5, CSS3, vanilla JavaScript only unless a dependency is truly required.
- No React, Next.js, Vue, Angular, Node backend, PHP, Docker, or cloud backend.

## Brand
- Brand: Darias
- Creator/developer/author: Derya Toklu only. Do not use any other personal name.
- Do not use unproven marketing claims.

## Content safety
- Empty URLs must disable or hide related actions.
- Missing screenshots: professional empty state, no fake UI shots.
- contactEmail empty: do not show a fake address.

## Quality
- Semantic HTML, accessibility, prefers-reduced-motion, visible focus.
- Fast, light, SEO-friendly, bilingual, scalable via central data files.
